From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 23:48:04 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] media: add the Darwin UML Virtio video encoder

The stateful V4L2 encoder for the Darwin host's Virtio video device with
ID 30, in the same driver as the decoder. The driver binds a device with
that ID only when it negotiates VIRTIO_VIDEO_F_V4L2_CONTROLS, names its
node "stateful-encoder", and numbers it from a vid_nr_enc parameter.

The device lists its controls with their types, ranges, defaults, menu
skip masks and flags, as V4L2 control IDs and menu indices. The driver
registers that list for each open file and forwards a value unchanged, so
a control the host learns needs no change here. A descriptor whose ID,
type or menu this kernel does not define the same way is skipped rather
than failing the open. The framework's table has no entry for some
booleans the UAPI names, PREPEND_SPSPPS_TO_IDR and
H264_HIERARCHICAL_CODING among them, and types them as integers, so a
boolean or button the device describes is registered as the device
describes it and every control the device publishes reaches the client.
A control the device does not mark dynamic is grabbed while the coded
queue streams, as the stateful encoder interface requires, and a control
is inactive for the coded formats its descriptor does not name.

The device creates its session at the first raw frame, from the formats
and controls it holds then. A raw frame therefore reaches the device only
while the coded queue streams and no drain holds the stream, and the
driver keeps it until then in queue order and returns it with STREAMOFF
or an error. ENCODER_CMD STOP drains: the next coded buffer is empty,
carries V4L2_BUF_FLAG_LAST and is announced by V4L2_EVENT_EOS, and a
STREAMOFF of the raw queue in a drain asks the device for that buffer
again. A buffer holding only parameter sets carries no frame-type flag.

The raw queue's formats follow the device: the ones it accepts with the
current coded format, a plane layout named by the device's plane count,
the line lengths the device reads, at the pitch a guest allocator gives
a buffer, which TRY_FMT predicts as S_FMT sets it, and the size the
visible rectangle gives the coded stream. A packed raw format is listed
under the name of its memory order, so RGBA8888 is RGBA32 ('AB24') where
the decoder's table keeps its older RGB32. The frame interval and the
colorimetry cross the wire in the stream-information commands.

The shared command paths gain what the encoder needs: a response length
for the commands whose answer varies, a slab cache name per device, and
the data size of a completed coded buffer.
