+The local port uses Linux 6.18 media APIs and the paired
+UML_VIRTIO_VIDEO_VERSION 1 host protocol. The decoder (device ID 31) exposes
+H.264, HEVC, and baseline JPEG with hardware-dependent profiles, including
+10-bit output. The canonical wire declarations are
+kernel/common/video/virtio_video.h in the owning Darwin host repository.
 
 A buffer reaches the device in a RESOURCE_ATTACH command with one scatter list
 per plane, and a list is as long as the buffer has physically separate pieces:
@@ -26,3 +26,33 @@ queue exported, guest memory from a heap or another driver, or one holding all
 of a buffer's planes, which follow one another at their negotiated sizes. The
 lengths a client states for the planes may be those sizes, the dma-buf's size
 or zero, because only the dma-buf bounds where the planes lie.
+
+The encoder (device ID 30) is a V4L2 stateful encoder (dev-encoder.rst) on
+the node "stateful-encoder", numbered from the vid_nr_enc parameter. The
+driver binds it only when the device offers VIRTIO_VIDEO_F_V4L2_CONTROLS.
+
+- Queues. V4L2 OUTPUT holds raw frames and CAPTURE holds coded buffers. The
+  coded format is set first; the raw formats then listed are the ones the
+  device accepts with it. A raw format the device takes both as one buffer
+  for all planes and as one buffer per plane is listed under both V4L2
+  names. The device decides the line lengths, at the pitch a guest allocator
+  gives a buffer, so a client's bytesperline is not a request the device
+  honors and TRY_FMT and S_FMT answer with the device's.
+- Visible rectangle. S_SELECTION CROP on OUTPUT is the coded size, which
+  CAPTURE reports. S_PARM sets the frame interval and S_FMT on OUTPUT the
+  colorimetry, both through the stream-information commands; CAPTURE reports
+  what the device writes.
+- Controls. The device lists its controls with their ranges, and the driver
+  registers exactly that list for each open file, skipping one it cannot
+  describe, and forwards values unchanged. A control the device does not
+  mark dynamic is grabbed while the CAPTURE queue streams, so it fails with
+  EBUSY. A control is inactive for a coded format its descriptor does not
+  name.
+- Starting and draining. The device creates its session at the first raw
+  frame, so a raw frame reaches it only while CAPTURE streams and no drain
+  holds the stream; until then the driver keeps the frame, and returns it
+  with STREAMOFF. ENCODER_CMD STOP drains: the device encodes what it has,
+  the next coded buffer is empty with V4L2_BUF_FLAG_LAST and V4L2_EVENT_EOS
+  is sent. START, or a restart of either queue, resumes. A coded buffer
+  holding only parameter sets (header mode SEPARATE) carries no frame-type
+  flag.
